A||||1||GT GT 87||Porting exhaust ports?||||1||
Z||000000||GT GT 87||10-18-2001||10:34 PM||||I am building a 3.2 motor ,(parts from Shaun 41178) with hotter cam ,CW headers , and modified heads. They are gasket matched on the intake side. Should I do the same on the exhaust side. No one seems to talk about exhaust ports , only intake ports ? What do you think ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||10-18-2001||10:58 PM||||Don't bother. By keeping the edge of the exhaust port uneven, you reduce back-flow back into the head. I.E., the exhaust gas moves forward reasonably inhindered into a larger space, and has to work against the flow to go back, if it has that 'lip' to overcome. The only thing I could see as having any merit would be polishing the inside of the exhaust outles by the valves, offering less resistance leaving the cylinders. <p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||10
